@startuml
title What "dominated" means when comparing configurations

top to bottom direction

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 10
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontColor #111827
skinparam ArrowColor #4B5563
skinparam ArrowFontColor #374151
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #4B5563
  FontColor #111827
  BackgroundColor #F8FAFC
}

rectangle "Configuration A" as a #DCFCE7
rectangle "Configuration B" as b #FECACA

rectangle "A drifts less\nlower mean KL divergence" as q #DBEAFE
rectangle "A costs less\nfewer cache bytes per token" as c #DBEAFE

rectangle "B is dominated\nworse on quality AND more expensive,\nso nothing about your budget would make you pick it" as dom #FEF3C7

a -down-> q
a -down-> c
b -down-> q : loses
b -down-> c : loses
q -down-> dom
c -down-> dom

note bottom of dom
  Ranking reports domination so you can
  discard options outright, instead of
  weighing every configuration by hand.
end note
@enduml
